#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

int bc_ping(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a ping request to the \f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R] instance on
\f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R] (channel 0) and waits for a pong response.
This function serves as a lightweight health check and keepalive
mechanism.
.PP
The ping/pong exchange verifies that:
.IP \(bu 2
The transport connection is still alive.
.IP \(bu 2
The server process is responsive.
.IP \(bu 2
The protocol framing is intact.
.PP
On the v2 protocol, the ping is sent as a JSON message
\f[CR]{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqping\(dq}\f[R] on \f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R].
The server responds with \f[CR]{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqpong\(dq}\f[R].
.PP
The function blocks until the pong response is received or the timeout
expires.
