.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The ping operation requires an authenticated connection.
Calling \f[CR]bc_ping\f[R] before \f[CR]bc_auth(3)\f[R] returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_AUTH\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The ping/pong exchange is a lightweight operation that does not execute
any shell commands or modify server state.
.IP \(bu 2
The default timeout for the pong response is 10 seconds.
If the server is under heavy load and cannot respond within this window,
\f[CR]bc_ping\f[R] returns \f[CR]BC_ERR_TIMEOUT\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A successful ping does not guarantee that subsequent
\f[CR]bc_eval(3)\f[R] calls will succeed \(en the server could become
unresponsive between the ping and the eval.
Use ping for general health monitoring, not as a pre\-flight check for
individual commands.
.IP \(bu 2
The function consumes exactly one pong message from the server.
If multiple pings are sent without reading responses (not possible
through this API, but possible with raw protocol access), the responses
queue up and may cause confusion.
